---
layout: base.njk
navActive: examples
pagination:
  data: examplesFlat
  size: 1
  addAllPagesToCollections: true
  alias: ex
permalink: "/examples/{{ ex.key }}/index.html"
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ ex.title }}"
  description: "{{ ex.lede }}"
---
{#-
  One example per page, as the design draws it: a rail of all eleven
  under their three headings with the one you are reading marked, a
  breadcrumb, the title in the display face, the lede, the transcript
  typed live with the tools it called linked to their reference, what
  it reads, the steps to set it up as buttons that go somewhere real, a
  gold Request access, and three more like it.

  Every tool named under a window is in the registry — the build links
  each one to its own heading and a test refuses a name it does not know.
-#}
<div class="siterail">
  <aside class="siterail__nav" data-siterail data-open="false">
    <button type="button" class="siterail__head" data-rail-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="examples-rail">
      <span class="siterail__head-title">Examples</span>
      <span class="siterail__head-here">{{ ex.label }}</span>
      <span class="siterail__head-meta">{{ ex.count }}<span class="siterail__head-chevron">{% icon "chevron-down", 17 %}</span></span>
    </button>
    <nav class="siterail__list" id="examples-rail" aria-label="Examples">
      {%- for g in examples %}
      <div class="rail__group">{{ g.group }}</div>
      {%- for c in g.cases %}
      <a class="rail__item{% if c.key == ex.key %} rail__item--on{% endif %}" href="/examples/{{ c.key }}"{% if c.key == ex.key %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{% icon c.icon, 18 %}{{ c.label }}</a>
      {%- endfor %}
      {%- endfor %}
    </nav>
    <div class="siterail__foot">
      Every example runs against recorded history. <a href="/data">See the corpus ›</a>
    </div>
  </aside>

  <div class="siterail__body">
    <div class="docs__crumb">
      <a href="/examples/play">Examples</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>{{ ex.group }}</span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="hero-title" style="font-size: 38px; margin: 0 0 10px">{{ ex.title }}</h1>
    <p class="docs__lede" style="max-width: 60ch; margin-bottom: 22px">{{ ex.lede | safe }}</p>
    <p class="footnote" style="margin: -12px 0 18px">A real exchange, recorded 2026-09-10 as King Thing of POAP KINGS: the tools under the window are the ones that answered, and every number came back from them.</p>

    <div style="display: flex; gap: 20px; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: flex-start">
      {%- if ex.script %}
      <div style="flex: 1 1 480px; min-width: 300px">
        {%- set scripts = [{ key: ex.key, label: ex.label, tool: ex.script.tool, lines: ex.script.lines }] %}
        {% include "transcript.njk" %}
      </div>
      {%- endif %}

      <div style="flex: 1 1 260px; min-width: 240px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
        <section class="panel">
          <div class="panel__head">What it reads</div>
          <div class="panel__body" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px">
            {%- for r in ex.reads %}
            <span style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--ink-body)">
              <span style="width: 5px; height: 5px; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--accent-bright); flex: 0 0 auto; margin-top: 7px"></span>{{ r | safe }}
            </span>
            {%- endfor %}
          </div>
        </section>
        <section class="panel">
          <div class="panel__head">To set this up</div>
          <div class="panel__body" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 9px">
            {%- for step in ex.setup %}
            <a class="btn" style="justify-content: space-between" href="{{ step | setupHref }}">{{ step | safe }} {% icon "arrow-right", 15 %}</a>
            {%- endfor %}
          </div>
        </section>
        <a class="btn btn--primary" style="justify-content: center" href="/signin?request">{% icon "user-plus", 16 %}Request access</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top: 26px; padding-top: 20px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line-soft)">
      <div class="label" style="margin-bottom: 12px">More like this</div>
      <div style="display: flex; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap">
        {%- for r in ex.related %}
        <a class="rail-card" href="/examples/{{ r.key }}">
          <span class="rail-card__title">{% icon r.icon, 17 %}{{ r.title }}</span>
          <span class="rail-card__lede">{{ r.lede | safe | truncate(110) }}</span>
        </a>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<script defer src="/assets/site-rail.js"></script>
<script defer src="/assets/transcript.js"></script>
